 "notes": "State-bucket settings (versioning, public access block, SSE-KMS) are bound to the bucket named my-terraform-state-bucket-<account>; the name check accepts a 12-digit suffix in the plan or a caller-identity/account reference in the declared text. Each inline grant is bound to its role: an aws_iam_role_policy that references the role (planned JSON or declared jsonencode text) or the role's inline_policy block. S3 access requires the bucket name plus object read and write actions in the same policy. 'any Lambda function'/'any Glue job run' require function:*/job/* or Resource \"*\". Gap: an inline policy whose JSON is unknown at plan and comes from an aws_iam_policy_document cannot be bound to its role, so it fails. Trust policies are core: the prompt states the trusting service for every role."
